                                "sense_id": "667ad852-dbc9-3f45-b04c-0ca57225fbba",
                                "text": "Here, too, the poet calls attention to Belial's role as one who blurs the borderline between essence and appearance: Belial himself seems fair (physically attractive), but is empty inside, and Milton was surely aware that in Hebrew the first syllable of the fallen angel's name means without."
